The {{Term/Store|Phantom Greaves|Phantom Greaves|Series, BotW, TotK}} are a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
Phantom Greaves are a piece of [[Armor]] exclusive to {{TMT}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack. Obtaining them is one part of the objective of the "[[EX Treasure: Phantasma]]" [[Side Quest]]. The Greaves were stolen from [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]] by [[Misko]] and a clue to their location can be found in [[Misko's EX Journal]] at the [[Outpost Ruins]].<ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal"/><ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal 2"/> The [[Treasure Chest]] that hides the Phantom Greaves can be found buried in the southeast of the [[Hyrule Garrison Ruins]] near a ruined [[Guardian Stalker]]. After obtaining the Phantom Greaves, [[Granté]] will begin selling them for 50 [[Rupee]]s.{{Note|Prior to the [[The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild#Updates|Version 1.3.3 Update]], Granté would not sell any Armor that is exclusive to the Expansion Pass or {{TMT}} Downloadable Content Pack. This meant that the Phantom Greaves could not be replaced if sold, which was noted in the description of the Greaves.<ref name="BotW Inventory 2"/>}}

According to its description, the Phantom Greaves look just like the Greaves supposedly worn by [[Phantom]]s that tormented heroes.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> When worn, the Phantom Greaves provide one level of [[Attack Up]]. The Phantom Greaves cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]] nor can they be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. The Phantom Greaves, alongside the [[Phantom Helmet]] and [[Phantom Armor]], compose the [[Phantom Equipment]].<ref name="CaC 188"/><ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/>

